{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788686262681,"sessionID":"ses_f89fe1261ffe8viTNFDooEJYor","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9921f9e1ddf528b5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git remote -v && git log --oneline -3 origin/main 2>/dev/null"},"output":"origin\thttps://github.com/kantord/toylang.git (fetch)\norigin\thttps://github.com/kantord/toylang.git (push)\n8011893 Land issue-172: Migrate binary-trees bench off the retired input keyword\n2fc273d Migrate binary-trees bench off the retired input keyword\nc5a3fe2 Merge origin/main into issue-172, resolve the landing conflicts\n","metadata":{"output":"origin\thttps://github.com/kantord/toylang.git (fetch)\norigin\thttps://github.com/kantord/toylang.git (push)\n8011893 Land issue-172: Migrate binary-trees bench off the retired input keyword\n2fc273d Migrate binary-trees bench off the retired input keyword\nc5a3fe2 Merge origin/main into issue-172, resolve the landing conflicts\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git remote -v && git log --oneline -3 origin/main 2>/dev/null","time":{"start":1788686262676,"end":1788686262679}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The issue id is `benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build`. The gh issue view with that name failed. Maybe the issue number is different. Let me try to find the issue. The board references `gh:NNN` for some. But benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build has no issue number. Let me try `gh issue view` with the board's row. Maybe the issue exists with a number. Let me look for how other issue-lanes map. Actually, the brief says run `gh issue view benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build`. Since that failed, maybe I should try a numeric lookup. Let me check the git remote and see if there's an issue number in recent commits or branch.\n\nLet me try `gh issue view 172` to understand the format, but 172 is binary-trees. Actually let me look at what issues exist. But gh issue list is denied. Only gh issue view <N> is allowed.\n\nLet me search the repo for the issue number for fannkuch. Maybe there's a mapping somewhere. Let me check ESCALATION.md and recent git log.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_07602606200146NFTh7PS6qRaM","sessionID":"ses_f89fe1261ffe8viTNFDooEJYor","messageID":"msg_0760249df001o2Mgp5dYDazOHD"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788686263633,"sessionID":"ses_f89fe1261ffe8viTNFDooEJYor","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8a33034f2bbb3e50","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build/ESCALATION.md"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build/ESCALATION.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Escalation: `just check` cannot go green as root\n2: \n3: ## Question\n4: \n5: The `search-layer-build` brief requires `just check` green. Two pre-existing tests,\n6: `tests/fmt_project.rs::unreadable_directory_is_reported_and_walk_continues` and\n7: `::unreadable_file_is_reported_and_walk_continues`, cannot pass when the suite runs as root:\n8: they chmod a directory or file to `0o000` and assert that the `toylang fmt` walker reports a\n9: permission error. Root bypasses permission bits, so `read_dir`/`read` succeed and the refusal\n10: never happens.\n11: \n12: ## Evidence it is environmental, not caused by this branch\n13: \n14: - The failing assertion is exactly `read_dir` on a `0o000` directory. Verified in this sandbox:\n15:   as root, `ls` reads the directory; as `nobody` (via `setpriv`), it gets `Permission denied`.\n16: - Running the already-built `fmt_project` test binary as `nobody` passes both tests unchanged.\n17: - CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs on `ubuntu-latest`, a non-root user, where both pass.\n18: \n19: None of this branch's changes (the `first`/`any`/`all` builtins) touch file permissions or the\n20: formatter.\n21: \n22: ## Alternatives\n23: \n24: 1. **Skip the two tests when running as root.** Minimal, transparent, keeps the assertions\n25:    fully active for the non-root case that CI and normal development run. The chosen path.\n26: 2. **Run the whole suite as a non-root user in this sandbox.** Requires giving a non-root user\n27:    write access to `/repo` (the suite rewrites `tests/corpus/*.yaml` and\n28:    `site/public/corpus.json` in place) and a copy of `CARGO_HOME`; invasive and fragile.\n29: 3. **Leave `just check` red and document only.** Fails the brief's explicit definition of done.\n30: \n31: ## Decision\n32: \n33: Took alternative 1: a `running_as_root()` guard (`id -u` reports 0) at the top of the two\n34: tests, with a comment explaining why the assertion is unobservable as root. The guard does not\n35: silently cover a broken walker: for any non-root user the tests run exactly as before. Revert\n36: this if the maintainer prefers a different accommodation.\n\n(End of file - total 36 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Escalation: `just check` cannot go green as root\n\n## Question\n\nThe `search-layer-build` brief requires `just check` green. Two pre-existing tests,\n`tests/fmt_project.rs::unreadable_directory_is_reported_and_walk_continues` and\n`::unreadable_file_is_reported_and_walk_continues`, cannot pass when the suite runs as root:\nthey chmod a directory or file to `0o000` and assert that the `toylang fmt` walker reports a\npermission error. Root bypasses permission bits, so `read_dir`/`read` succeed and the refusal\nnever happens.\n\n## Evidence it is environmental, not caused by this branch\n\n- The failing assertion is exactly `read_dir` on a `0o000` directory. Verified in this sandbox:\n  as root, `ls` reads the directory; as `nobody` (via `setpriv`), it gets `Permission denied`.\n- Running the already-built `fmt_project` test binary as `nobody` passes both tests unchanged.\n- CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs on `ubuntu-latest`, a non-root user, where both pass.\n\nNone of this branch's changes (the `first`/`any`/`all` builtins) touch file permissions or the\nformatter.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build/ESCALATION.md","text":"# Escalation: `just check` cannot go green as root\n\n## Question\n\nThe `search-layer-build` brief requires `just check` green. Two pre-existing tests,\n`tests/fmt_project.rs::unreadable_directory_is_reported_and_walk_continues` and\n`::unreadable_file_is_reported_and_walk_continues`, cannot pass when the suite runs as root:\nthey chmod a directory or file to `0o000` and assert that the `toylang fmt` walker reports a\npermission error. Root bypasses permission bits, so `read_dir`/`read` succeed and the refusal\nnever happens.\n\n## Evidence it is environmental, not caused by this branch\n\n- The failing assertion is exactly `read_dir` on a `0o000` directory. Verified in this sandbox:\n  as root, `ls` reads the directory; as `nobody` (via `setpriv`), it gets `Permission denied`.\n- Running the already-built `fmt_project` test binary as `nobody` passes both tests unchanged.\n- CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs on `ubuntu-latest`, a non-root user, where both pass.\n\nNone of this branch's changes (the `first`/`any`/`all` builtins) touch file permissions or the\nformatter.\n\n## Alternatives\n\n1. **Skip the two tests when running as root.** Minimal, transparent, keeps the assertions\n   fully active for the non-root case that CI and normal development run. The chosen path.\n2. **Run the whole suite as a non-root user in this sandbox.** Requires giving a non-root user\n   write access to `/repo` (the suite rewrites `tests/corpus/*.yaml` and\n   `site/public/corpus.json` in place) and a copy of `CARGO_HOME`; invasive and fragile.\n3. **Leave `just check` red and document only.** Fails the brief's explicit definition of done.\n\n## Decision\n\nTook alternative 1: a `running_as_root()` guard (`id -u` reports 0) at the top of the two\ntests, with a comment explaining why the assertion is unobservable as root. The guard does not\nsilently cover a broken walker: for any non-root user the tests run exactly as before. Revert\nthis if the maintainer prefers a different accommodation.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":36,"totalLines":36,"truncated":false}},"title":"ESCALATION.md","time":{"start":1788686263624,"end":1788686263630}},"id":"prt_07602618a0014S4dA7Kb7T29Vq","sessionID":"ses_f89fe1261ffe8viTNFDooEJYor","messageID":"msg_0760249df001o2Mgp5dYDazOHD"}}
