{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788686274949,"sessionID":"ses_f89fe1261ffe8viTNFDooEJYor","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b826d44bc47dee4b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls -R benches"},"output":"benches:\ninputs\nprograms\n\nbenches/inputs:\nbinary-trees.txt\n\nbenches/programs:\nbinary-trees.toy\n","metadata":{"output":"benches:\ninputs\nprograms\n\nbenches/inputs:\nbinary-trees.txt\n\nbenches/programs:\nbinary-trees.toy\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"ls -R benches","time":{"start":1788686274945,"end":1788686274947}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The ESCALATION.md is from a different lane (search-layer-build), so it's inherited context. I should not treat it as mine. \n\nThe gh issue view with the issue id failed. The issue may not have a number associated. Since the brief says read every comment before touching anything, and I can't find the issue via the id... Let me try to find the issue number. The binary-trees issue was gh:172. Let me try gh issue view with a number. Maybe the fannkuch issue has a number. But I can't search. \n\nLet me try `gh issue view` on the repo to see if there's a way. Actually the brief explicitly gave the command `gh issue view benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build`, which failed with \"invalid issue format\". This suggests the issue is referenced by its number somewhere. Let me check if there's a mapping. Perhaps the issue number is embedded in the branch name pattern or somewhere in plans.\n\nActually, since the issue isn't findable via gh, and the board row fully describes the task (it's a detailed spec in the brief + board), I can proceed based on the board row description and the brief, which together are the spec. The brief is essentially the full task description. The gh issue view is meant for context, but the board row and brief contain the substance.\n\nLet me try to find the issue number anyway. Let me look at git for \"fannkuch\" or check if there's an issue referenced. Let me check the branch naming - the worktree dir is issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build, branch issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build. \n\nLet me try gh issue view with a guess. Actually I shouldn't guess. Let me check if the issue exists by trying common approaches. The board row has no `issue:` field for this row (unlike others). So this lane may not have a gh issue yet, or the issue id IS the name. \n\nGiven the denial on gh issue list/search, and the failed view, I'll proceed with the board row + brief as the spec. The brief is very detailed. Let me now read the existing pattern.\n\nLet me look at benches/programs/binary-trees.toy and its corpus/bench counterparts.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_076029043001danOMafXkWvAe4","sessionID":"ses_f89fe1261ffe8viTNFDooEJYor","messageID":"msg_07602657d001xxBDvl91XVfOk2"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788686275209,"sessionID":"ses_f89fe1261ffe8viTNFDooEJYor","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-90645fa85169b9b8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build/justfile"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build/justfile</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # List available recipes.\n2: default:\n3:     @just --list\n4: \n5: # The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\n6: test:\n7:     cargo nextest run\n8: \n9: # The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\n10: check:\n11:     cargo nextest run -E 'not test(every_fragment_is_a_real_program)'\n12: \n13: # Opt-in: run the skipped Euler 8/11/13/18 programs against real puzzle data in DIR, outside\n14: # `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\n15: euler-data DIR:\n16:     EULER_DATA={{DIR}} cargo nextest run --run-ignored ignored-only -E 'test(euler_real_data)'\n17: \n18: # Re-run the slow-fragment tier: the same suite, but `slow` fragments are executed on every\n19: # backend rather than only type-checked and emitted. The tier exists so `just test` stays fast;\n20: # this is where the deferred execution claim is re-verified.\n21: slow-test:\n22:     TOYLANG_SLOW=1 cargo nextest run\n23: \n24: # Run clippy with the repo's lint set, the same surface the Stop hook checks.\n25: clippy:\n26:     cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets\n27: \n28: # Time one benchmark (a name under benches/programs/) across every backend with hyperfine.\n29: # Design: plans/benchmark-plan.md. Results land in benches/results/<name>.{md,json}.\n30: bench NAME:\n31:     cargo run -q --bin bench -- {{NAME}}\n32: \n33: # Formatter check over every .toy file from the repo root down (exit 1 on drift).\n34: fmt:\n35:     cargo run -q -- fmt\n36: \n37: # Rewrite drifted files in place (same exit code as the check).\n38: fmt-write:\n39:     cargo run -q -- fmt --write\n40: \n41: # The repo's mechanical checks, the same surface the Stop hook runs.\n42: checks:\n43:     bash .claude/checks/run.sh\n44: \n45: # The autonomous drive loop: a tick every 600s, live colorized output, Ctrl-C to stop. Run ONE.\n46: drive:\n47:     .claude/scripts/drive-loop.sh\n48: \n49: # Fire one coordinator tick right now (zero tokens if there is nothing to do).\n50: tick:\n51:     .claude/scripts/drive-tick.sh\n52: \n53: # Watch the current coordinator tick live (detaches with Ctrl-C, tick untouched).\n54: peek:\n55:     .claude/scripts/tick-peek.sh\n\n(End of file - total 55 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# List available recipes.\ndefault:\n    @just --list\n\n# The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\ntest:\n    cargo nextest run\n\n# The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\ncheck:\n    cargo nextest run -E 'not test(every_fragment_is_a_real_program)'\n\n# Opt-in: run the skipped Euler 8/11/13/18 programs against real puzzle data in DIR, outside\n# `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\neuler-data DIR:\n    EULER_DATA={{DIR}} cargo nextest run --run-ignored ignored-only -E 'test(euler_real_data)'\n\n# Re-run the slow-fragment tier: the same suite, but `slow` fragments are executed on every\n# backend rather than only type-checked and emitted. The tier exists so `just test` stays fast;\n# this is where the deferred execution claim is re-verified.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fannkuch-redux-build/justfile","text":"# List available recipes.\ndefault:\n    @just --list\n\n# The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\ntest:\n    cargo nextest run\n\n# The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\ncheck:\n    cargo nextest run -E 'not test(every_fragment_is_a_real_program)'\n\n# Opt-in: run the skipped Euler 8/11/13/18 programs against real puzzle data in DIR, outside\n# `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\neuler-data DIR:\n    EULER_DATA={{DIR}} cargo nextest run --run-ignored ignored-only -E 'test(euler_real_data)'\n\n# Re-run the slow-fragment tier: the same suite, but `slow` fragments are executed on every\n# backend rather than only type-checked and emitted. The tier exists so `just test` stays fast;\n# this is where the deferred execution claim is re-verified.\nslow-test:\n    TOYLANG_SLOW=1 cargo nextest run\n\n# Run clippy with the repo's lint set, the same surface the Stop hook checks.\nclippy:\n    cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets\n\n# Time one benchmark (a name under benches/programs/) across every backend with hyperfine.\n# Design: plans/benchmark-plan.md. Results land in benches/results/<name>.{md,json}.\nbench NAME:\n    cargo run -q --bin bench -- {{NAME}}\n\n# Formatter check over every .toy file from the repo root down (exit 1 on drift).\nfmt:\n    cargo run -q -- fmt\n\n# Rewrite drifted files in place (same exit code as the check).\nfmt-write:\n    cargo run -q -- fmt --write\n\n# The repo's mechanical checks, the same surface the Stop hook runs.\nchecks:\n    bash .claude/checks/run.sh\n\n# The autonomous drive loop: a tick every 600s, live colorized output, Ctrl-C to stop. Run ONE.\ndrive:\n    .claude/scripts/drive-loop.sh\n\n# Fire one coordinator tick right now (zero tokens if there is nothing to do).\ntick:\n    .claude/scripts/drive-tick.sh\n\n# Watch the current coordinator tick live (detaches with Ctrl-C, tick untouched).\npeek:\n    .claude/scripts/tick-peek.sh","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":55,"totalLines":55,"truncated":false}},"title":"justfile","time":{"start":1788686275179,"end":1788686275191}},"id":"prt_076029179001N3POGBbItLbIQV","sessionID":"ses_f89fe1261ffe8viTNFDooEJYor","messageID":"msg_07602657d001xxBDvl91XVfOk2"}}
